<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 27px; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 29px; padding-bottom: 20px; width: 100%;"> <p style="margin: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 27px; line-height: 29px; color: #0f476b;">Flywire Dashboard:</span></p> </td> 
</tr> 
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" class="aligned-bullets" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 14px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 21px; padding-bottom: 40px; width: 100%;"> 
<ul style="margin-bottom: 0px !important; margin-top: 0px !important;"> 
<li style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 23px;">Our Flywire Dashboard is now available in Italian. For those looking to change the language to Italian, go to the user and click My Account. Select Italian as your supported language from the drop-down menu and click Save.</li> 
<li style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 23px;">You can now view chargeback disputes directly within your Dashboard. Chargeback information appears in a new ‘Chargeback Disputes’ tab alongside ‘Payments’ and ‘Disbursements’ in the Incoming Payments module and shows chargeback disputes, statuses and deadline to submit defense documents. Within the ‘Payments’ tab we have also added a blinking orange dot icon to highlight each payment that has a chargeback associated with it. In addition to now being able to see this information in the Dashboard, you will continue to receive emails from Flywire about chargeback details and any necessary action required.</li> 
</ul> </td> 
</tr> 
</tbody>
</table> </td> 
</tr> 
</tbody>
</table> </td> 
</tr> 
</tbody>
</table> </td> 
</tr> 
</tbody>
</table> </td> 
</tr> 
<tr> 
